## Supabase Storage: Cost and Capacity Estimates

Supabase's free tier includes **1 GB of storage**.

Estimated time before reaching the free tier limit, depending on report size:

| Average report size | Approximate page count | Reports per year | Years until 1 GB is full |
|---|---|---|---|
| 10 MB (large/image-heavy) | ~100–200 pages | 70 | ~1.5 years |
| 5 MB (typical PDF) | ~50–100 pages | 70 | ~3 years |
| 2 MB (text-heavy PDF) | ~20–50 pages | 70 | ~7 years |

When the free tier is eventually exceeded, Supabase's Pro plan costs $25/month and includes 100 GB — far more than this project would likely need for the foreseeable future. Given the supervisor's guidance not to over-engineer at this stage, the free tier is a reasonable starting point.

---

## Summary Recommendation

Given the current website structure (Quarto + GitHub Pages) and the stated security goal of reasonable access control for sensitive-but-not-classified institutional reports, the recommended approach is:

- **Client-only authentication** via Supabase for user login
- **Supabase Storage** (not GitHub Pages) for storing all reports, with access rules configured so only authenticated users can retrieve files

This approach requires no new infrastructure, fits within Supabase's free tier, and provides meaningful protection appropriate to the sensitivity level of the data.
